sample_prompt:
You are an advanced information extraction system specialized in understanding and parsing prescriptions. Your task is to carefully analyze the given image and the text in the image, and extract relevant details to populate a JSON object following the provided schema.

JSON Schema:
```json
{
    "prescription_elements": {
        "drug": [
            {
                "name": "string",                        // The name of the medicine or drug in the prescription
                "generic": "string",                     // The generic name of the medicine, i.e., the combination of drugs the medicine is made up of
                "frequency": "string",                   // The frequency at which the medicine is prescribed, e.g., 1-0-1, 0-1-1-0, 1-0-0-0-1, etc.
                "dosage": "string",                      // The amount of the medicine or tablet that should be taken by the patient
                "medication_time": "string",             // When the patient should take the medicine, e.g., Before Meal, Empty Stomach, 8am 3pm 9pm, etc.
                "duration": "string"                     // The number of days or duration for which the patient should take the medicine
            }
        ], // This should only contain the medicines that are prescribed in the given prescription.
        "current_medication": [],               // Medicines currently being used by the patient
        "symptoms": [],                         // Symptoms of the patient as mentioned in the prescription
        "diagnosis": [],                        // Diagnosis of the patient as mentioned in the prescription
        "vitals": [
            {
                "name": "string",
                "value": "string",
                "unit": "string"
            }
        ],  // A list of dictionaries for all the vitals, readings, and investigations mentioned in the prescription
        "labtests": [],                         // Names of the lab tests or studies prescribed in the prescription
        "findings": [],                         // Any findings about the patient in the prescription
        "lifestyle": [],                        // The patient's lifestyle habits, such as 'smoker', 'drinks alcohol', etc.
        "advice": "string",                     // Any advice or suggestions given to the patient
        "medical_history": [],                  // Any past chronic conditions or surgeries undergone by the patient
        "family_medical_history": []            // Any medical conditions or diseases in the patient's family, e.g., diabetes, hypertension, etc.
    }
}```

You are an advanced information extraction system specialized in understanding various medical lab reports. Your task is to carefully analyze the given image and the text in the image, and extract relevant details to populate a JSON object following the provided schema.

JSON Schema:
```json
{
    "lab_report_elements": {
        "tests": [
            {
                "test_name": "string",         // Name of the test
                "values": [                    // There could be multiple values for the same test on different dates mentioned in the document
                    {
                        "value": "string",     // Value for the test provided in the document
                        "context": {
                            "type": "string",  // If a date is associated with the test value, then type is `date`; if there is a specific column name associated with the value (e.g., 'mean', 'std', '%', etc.), mark it as `other`; else null
                            "name": "string"   // If the type is `date`, then fill it with the mentioned date and time if time is also provided; if the type is `other`, fill it with the column name associated with the value; else null
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "range": "string",             // Normal range for the test as provided in the document
                "unit": "string",              // Unit for the test as provided in the document
                "panel_name": "string",        // Panel name that might be mentioned on top of a group of tests (e.g., CBC, Urinalysis, etc.)
                "specimen": {
                    "value": "string",         // Specimen is the sample on which the test is conducted; it might be mentioned in the report either with each test or for a group of tests. e.g (blood, urine, stool, etc.)
                    "source": "string"         // Valid values for specimen source are `test_name`, `panel_name`, `sample_name`, and `inferred`
                },
                "method": "string"             // Method of the test as mentioned in the document
            }
        ]
    }
}

```
Additional instructions:
1. If certain information is not explicitly provided, mark it as null in the JSON, except for the specimen, which can be inferred.
2. The specimen source should be test_name if the specimen is mentioned with the test name, panel_name if it is mentioned with the panel name, sample_name if it is mentioned anywhere else on the page, inferred if it is deduced from the context (e.g., surrounding tests, value, unit, range, method, etc.), or null if it cannot be determined. Follow this priority order: test_name > panel_name > sample_name > inferred > null.

